            <ArticleTitle>[Ruptured pedicled myoma node with hemoperitoneum].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>547-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report on an extremely rare complication observed by them in association with uterus myomatosus, namely, rupture of a pedunculated myoma node during an examination under anaesthesia with subsequent haemoperitoneum. Basing on this case report, rare but dramatic complications in uterus myomatosus are recalled.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
